      "title": "MacMax - READ ME FIRST",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MacMax - MiniMax H3 for Apple Silicon\n\n*(MacMax = Mac + MiniMax. Any Apple Silicon Mac with enough unified memory. It is not a\nMax-chip requirement.)*\n\nVideo with native stereo audio in one pass, running locally on a Mac. Smallest graph that\nstill does T2V / I2V / FLF, tuned to measured numbers rather than to the stock template's\ndefaults (which are presumably tuned for CUDA cards, where they may well be right).\n\n**Memory:** the DiT is ~20 GB and the encoder ~15 GB, loaded in sequence. Tested at 48 GB.\n32 GB is untested and expected to be tight; under 32 GB is not recommended. Reports from\nother configurations welcome.\n\n**Expect ~35 min** for the default 0.6 MP @ 5s / 20 steps, with Spectrum on as shipped\n(~47 min if you bypass it).\n**Step 1 takes several minutes on its own** because the text encoder loads first - it is not\nhung. The seed widget ships on `randomize`; pin it to 6120072732051 to compare against our\nnumbers.\n\n**New here? Read the green SETUP panel on the right first** (four model files, three custom\nnodes, one launch flag). Then edit only the blue `1 - EDIT THESE` column and hit Run.\n\n**Toggles.** Everything optional in this graph toggles the same way: select the node,\npress **Ctrl+B** (bypass). Purple = off. No switch nodes, no extra packs.\n- the two `LoadImage` nodes: both off = **T2V** (default), first on = **I2V**, both on = **FLF**\n  (no R2V here - identity-from-reference-stills is a different conditioning node; use the\n  Foxydit port that ships alongside)\n- `Spectrum`: ships **ON** (-27%, faces hold). Bypass it for a pure uncached reference\n- `EasyCache`: ships OFF and should stay off, see below. **Never run both at once**\n- the `EXTRAS` column: audio preview (on), 1080x1920 export + audio stem (off)\n\n**Troubleshooting.** Model loaders red on first load = your models sit in subfolders;\nre-pick the four files once. That is the only expected error. If the GGUF loader is missing,\n`pip install gguf==0.18.0` into the ComfyUI venv and restart with `ASFP8_INT8_EXT=1`.\n\n**Why 0.6 MP @ 5s.** Cost is a **token budget**, not a resolution or a length limit:\ntokens ~ megapixels x seconds. Measured, 20 steps:\n\n| config | tokens | s/step | note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.03 MP @ 3s | ~22k | 131.6 | comfortable |\n| **0.6 MP @ 5s** | **~22k** | **137.8** | **near-identical cost, longer shots** |\n| 1.03 MP @ 5s | ~37k | ~340 | ~3x wall clock, near the memory floor |\n\nThose are sampling-only rates, uncached, so they are comparable to each other. Wall clock per\nstep is higher because it carries model load and decode.\n\n**Spectrum ships ON, EasyCache ships OFF.** Both skip sampling steps, but not the same way,\nand it shows. Same seed, same prompt, same 0.6 MP/5s canvas, measured on face crops resized\nto a common size so resolution cannot win for free:\n\n| | wall | fine detail | faces |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| uncached | 47:21 | 0.381 | reference |\n| EasyCache 0.2 | 31:16 | **0.405** | mouths and teeth visibly smeared |\n| **Spectrum d1** | **34:27** | 0.368 | **teeth and lips hold, no artefacts** |\n\nNote EasyCache scores the **highest** on fine detail while looking the **worst**. It is not\nresolving detail, it is injecting spurious high-frequency edge noise, so any sharpness metric\nblesses it. This is the trap the earlier version of this pack fell into: it recommended\nEasyCache on a 0.991 layout correlation computed on thumbnails that cannot see a mouth.\n\nSpectrum *forecasts* the skipped steps from a fitted curve instead of reusing a cached state,\nwhich is why fast-changing detail survives. Measured here: 8 of 20 steps forecast. It costs\n~3 min more than EasyCache and is worth it on anything with a face. EasyCache stays in the\ngraph as a one-keypress option for faceless b-roll, where the artefacts have nothing to\ndamage. **Never enable both** - Spectrum's author is explicit about this.\n\n**Steps: 20.** 15 and 20 show no measurable difference at this metric's resolution (0.940\nboth, vs the uncached 20-step reference) because they evaluate a similar number of real steps.\nBelow ~6 steps **speech breaks before video does** - at 4 steps\nthe picture is clean but dialogue loops or vanishes. Judge audio at 10+ steps only.\n\n**Sigma shift** is stock 12/3. The Turbo LoRA workflow wants 12/6. I could not get that LoRA\nto load on this machine (it OOMs at runtime regardless of canvas), but others report it\nworking, so treat that as my setup rather than a property of the model.\n\nNo triton, no SageAttention, nothing CUDA. None of it has an Apple Silicon build.\n\n---\n**MacMax** by MAD IT. Built on ComfyUI's shipped `video_minimax_h3_t2v` template - the graph\nis that template flattened, so nothing here is a reimplementation. Numbers above are from\n~40 measured renders on a single 48 GB M5 Pro; treat them as a strong prior, not a law.\nOne companion workflow for Apple Silicon ships alongside this one: a port of\n**foxfuressence**'s filmmaking rig."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
